Falsifies `timetable::proofs::a_time_of_day_is_strictly_later_and_listed`.

The defect: the mask keeps minutes at or after `after` rather than strictly after it, so a poll at the fire's own minute answers that minute again.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!((t as i32) > after)`, where `t == after`.

